efield. If this spell was cast from a graveyard, you may copy this spell and may choose a new target for the copy.\\nFlashback {4}{W} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Return up to three target artifacts and/or creatures to their owners' hands.\\nYou may cast a spell with mana value 4 or less from your hand without paying its mana cost.", 'Return up to three target land cards from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped. Create that many 4/2 green Plant Warrior creature tokens with reach.\\nFlashback {6}{G}{G} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Scry 1.\\nDraw a card.', 'Scry 2, then draw a card. (To scry 2, look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom and the rest on top in any order.)', 'Search your library for a Forest card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the other into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to two land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle. Then if you control three or more Deserts, create two 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.', "Slither Blade can't be blocked.", "Smoldering Stagecoach's power is equal to the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard.\\nWhenever Smoldering Stagecoach attacks, the next instant spell and the next sorcery spell you cast this turn each have cascade.\\nCrew 2", "Spells you cast but don't own cost {1} less to cast.\\nWhenever one or more creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, look at the top card of that player's library, then exile it face down. You may play that card for as long as it remains exiled, and mana of any type can be spent to cast that spell.", 'Storm-Kiln Artist gets +1/+0 for each artifact you control.\\nMagecraft — Whenever you cast or copy an instant or sorcery spell, create a Treasure token.', 'Sulfur Falls enters the battlefield tapped unless you control an Island or a Mountain.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Target opponent chooses X cards from their hand. Look at those cards. You may cast a spell from among them without paying its mana cost.', 'Target opponent exiles cards from the top of their library until they exile a nonland card. Until end of turn, you may cast that card without paying its mana cost.', 'Target opponent exiles the top X cards of their library. You may cast any number of spells with mana value X or less from among them without paying their mana costs.', 'Target player draws two cards.\\nFlashback—{1}{U}, Pay 3 life. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', 'Temple of Deceit enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Deceit enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', 'Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Temple of Malady enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Malady enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'Temple of Malice enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Malice enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', 'Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Temple of Silence enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Silence enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', 'Temple of Triumph enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Triumph enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', "The owner of target permanent shuffles it into their library, then reveals the top card of their library. If it's a permanent card, they put it onto the battlefield.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nFlying\\nWhenever you draw a card, Niv-Mizzet, Parun deals 1 damage to any target.\\nWhenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell, you draw a card.", 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each land card in your graveyard.\\nVigilance, reach, trample\\nWhen Rumbleweed enters the battlefield, other creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each land card in your graveyard.\\nWhenever Yuma, Proud Protector enters the battlefield or attacks, you may sacrifice a land. If you do, draw a card.\\nWhenever a Desert card is put into your graveyard from anywhere, create a 4/2 green Plant Warrior creature token with reach.', 'This spell costs {2} less to cast for each different mana value among instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard.\\nFlying, prowess\\nWhenever you cast your second spell each turn, create a 4/4 red Dragon Elemental creature token with flying and prowess.', 'This spell costs {8} less to cast if you have eight or more instant and/or sorcery cards in your graveyard.\\nWard {8}\\nMagecraft — Whenever you cast or copy an instant or sorcery spell, target creature has base power and toughness 8/8 until end of turn.', "Triton Shorestalker can't be blocked.", 'Undaunted (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each opponent.)\\nDestroy two target creatures.', 'Unholy Heat deals 2 damage to target creature or planeswalker.\\nDelirium — Unholy Heat deals 6 damage instead if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard.', 'Until end of turn, creatures you control gain menace and "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, exile the top card of that player\'s library face down. You may look at and play that card for as long as it remains exiled, and you may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast that spell."', 'Until end of turn, outlaw creatures you control get +1/+0 and gain "{T}: This creature deals damage equal to its power to target creature." (Assassins, Mercenaries, Pirates, Rogues, and Warlocks are outlaws.)', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Sun Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may return target permanent card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'When Avenger of Zendikar enters the battlefield, create a 0/1 green Plant creature token for each land you control.\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may put a +1/+1 counter on each Plant creature you control.', 'When Bitter Reunion enters the battlefield, you may discard a card. If you do, draw two cards.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Bitter Reunion: Creatures you control gain haste until end of turn.', 'When Charred Graverobber enters the battlefield, return target outlaw card from your graveyard to your hand.\\nEscape—{3}{B}{B}, Exile four other cards from your graveyard. (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its escape cost.)\\nCharred Graverobber escapes with a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'When Eccentric Farmer enters the battlefield, mill three cards, then you may return a land card from your graveyard to your hand. (To mill a card, put the top card of your library into your graveyard.)', 'When Elvish Rejuvenator enters the battlefield, look at the top five cards of your library. You may put a land card from among them onto the battlefield tapped. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'When Hostage Taker enters the battlefield, exile another target creature or artifact until Hostage Taker leaves the battlefield. You may cast that card for as long as it remains exiled, and mana of any type can be spent to cast that spell.', 'When Impulsive Pilferer dies, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")\\nEncore {3}{R} ({3}{R}, Exile this card from your graveyard: For each opponent, create a token copy that attacks that opponent this turn if able. They gain haste. Sacrifice them at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only as a sorcery.)', 'When Nantuko Cultivator enters the battlefield, you may discard any number of land cards. Put that many +1/+1 counters on Nantuko Cultivator and draw that many cards.', 'When Rain of Riches enters the battlefield, create two Treasure tokens.\\nThe first spell you cast each turn that mana from a Treasure was spent to cast has cascade. (When you cast the spell, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom in a random order.)', 'When Sand Scout enters the battlefield, if an opponent controls more lands than you, search your library for a Desert card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhenever one or more land cards are put into your graveyard from anywhere, create a 1/1 red, green, and white Sand Warrior creature token. This ability triggers only once each turn.', 'When Satyr Wayfinder enters the battlefield, reveal the top four cards of your library. You may put a land card from among them into your hand. Put the rest into your graveyard.', 'When Savvy Trader enters the battlefield, exile target permanent card from your graveyard. You may play that card for as long as it remains exiled.\\nSpells you cast from anywhere other than your hand cost {1} less to cast.', 'When Springbloom Druid enters the battlefield, you may sacrifice a land. If you do, search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'When Tenured Inkcaster enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.\\nWhenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it attacks, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'When Titania, Protector of Argoth enters the battlefield, return target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nWhenever a land you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, create a 5/3 green Elemental creature token.', "When Whirler Rogue enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature tokens with flying.\\nTap two untapped artifacts you control: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'When you cast this spell, reveal the top X cards of your library. You may put a nonland permanent card with mana value X or less from among them onto the battlefield. Then shuffle the rest into your library.\\nGenesis Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', 'When you cast this spell, target opponent exiles the top four cards of their library, then you may put any number of land cards that player owns from exile onto the battlefield under your control.', 'When you next cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn, copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.\\nFlashback {1}{U}{R} (You may cast this card from your graveyard for its flashback cost. Then exile it.)', "Whenever Ghostly Pilferer becomes untapped, you may pay {2}. If you do, draw a card.\\nWhenever an opponent casts a spell from anywhere other than their hand, draw a card.\\nDiscard a card: Ghostly Pilferer can't be blocked this turn.", 'Whenever Scaretiller becomes tapped, choose one —\\n• You may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield tapped.\\n• Return target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', 'Whenever World Shaper attacks, you may mill three cards.\\nWhen World Shaper dies, return all land cards from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', 'Whenever a creature an opponent controls dies, exile it with a hit counter on it.\\nAssassins, Mercenaries, and Rogues you control have deathtouch and "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, you may remove a hit counter from a card that player owns in exile. If you do, draw a card and create two Treasure tokens."', 'Whenever a creature deals combat damage to one of your opponents, its controller may draw a card.', "Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to a player, choose one —\\n• Goad target creature that player controls.\\n• Exile the top card of that player's library. Until end of turn, you may cast that card and you may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast that spell.", "Whenever an opponent attacks you and/or one or more planeswalkers you control, exile the top card of that player's library. You may play that card for as long as it remains exiled, and you may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast it.", "Whenever an opponent casts their first spell each turn, that player exiles the top card of their library. If it's a nonland card, you may cast it without paying its mana cost.", 'Whenever another nontoken creature dies, you may create a 1/1 black Rat creature token.\\nRats you control have deathtouch.', 'Whenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, look at the top card of their library, then exile it face down. For as long as it remains exiled, you may play it, and mana of any type can be spent to cast that spell.\\nEquip {1}', 'Whenever one or more land cards are put into your graveyard from anywhere, create a 0/1 green Plant creature token.\\n{G}, Sacrifice three creatures: Return target land card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Whenever one or more other creatures die, draw a card. This ability triggers only once each turn.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, create a 1/1 colorless Soldier artifact creature token.', "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, create an X/X blue Shark creature token with flying, where X is that spell's mana value.\\nCycling {X}{1}{U} ({X}{1}{U}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)\\nWhen you cycle Shark Typhoon, create an X/X blue Shark creature token with flying.", 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Guttersnipe deals 2 damage to each opponent.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 blue Bird Illusion creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 red Elemental creature token.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 2/2 blue Drake creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast your first instant or sorcery spell each turn, exile an instant or sorcery card at random from your graveyard. Then copy each card exiled with Arcane Bombardment. You may cast any number of the copies without paying their mana costs.', "Whenever you cast your second spell each turn, exile the top card of your library. Until the end of your next turn, you may play that card.\\n{T}: Copy target instant or sorcery spell you control. You may choose new targets for the copy. Activate only if you've cast three or more spells this turn.", "Will of the council — Starting with you, each player votes for a nonland permanent you don't control. Exile each permanent with the most votes or tied for most votes.", 'Woodland Cemetery enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Swamp or a Forest.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'You gain 2 life. Then you may discard two cards. If you do, draw three cards.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', "You may cast target instant or sorcery card from an opponent's graveyard without paying its mana cost. If that spell would be put into their graveyard, exile it instead.\\nCipher (Then you may exile this spell card encoded on a creature you control. Whenever that creature deals combat damage to a player, its controller may cast a copy of the encoded card without paying its mana cost.)", 'You may cast up to one target instant card and/or up to one target sorcery card from your graveyard each with mana value X or less without paying their mana costs. If a spell cast this way would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead. If X is 10 or more, copy each of those spells twice. You may choose new targets for the copies.', "You may pay {1}{B} rather than pay this spell's mana cost.\\nIf the {1}{B} cost was paid, an opponent draws a card.\\nExile target creature or planeswalker.", 'You may play an additional land on each of your turns.\\nPlay with the top card of your library revealed.\\nYou may play lands from the top of your library.', 'You may play an additional land this turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'You may play lands from your graveyard.', 'You may play lands from your graveyard.\\nUnearth {G}{G} ({G}{G}: Return this card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It gains haste. Exile it at the beginning of the next end step or if it would leave the battlefield. Unearth only as a sorcery.)', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Mill a card. You may put an instant or sorcery card milled this way into your hand.\\nTap an untapped legendary creature you control: Untap Leyline Dowser.', '{3}{R}: Gain control of target creature an opponent controls until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery.', "{4}, {T}: Target opponent exiles cards from the top of their library until they exile an instant or sorcery card. You may cast that card without paying its mana cost. Then put the exiled cards that weren't cast this way on the bottom of that library in a random order.", '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature.\\n{T}, Remove a counter from a creature you control: Create a Treasure token.\\n{T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Create a 2/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying.\\n{3}{B}: Untap Fain, the Broker.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{1}, {T}: Put a bounty counter on target creature. Activate only as a sorcery.\\nWhenever a creature with a bounty counter on it dies, each of its controller's opponents draws a card and gains 2 life.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\nWhen Dunes of the Dead is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Demolition Field: Destroy target nonbasic land an opponent controls. That land's controller may search their library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle. You may search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Exile all graveyards.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{R}{W}, {T}: Target creature gains double strike until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{W}{B}, {T}: Creatures you control gain deathtouch and lifelink until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you control a creature with power 4 or greater.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}, {T}: Target creature with power 3 or less can't be blocked this turn.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{B/G}, {T}: Add {B}{B}, {B}{G}, or {G}{G}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{G/U}, {T}: Add {G}{G}, {G}{U}, or {U}{U}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R/W}, {T}: Add {R}{R}, {R}{W}, or {W}{W}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add {G}.\\n{1}{G}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add {R}.\\n{2}{R}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Ramunap Ruins deals 2 damage to each opponent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add {W}.\\n{2}{W}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Command Beacon: Put your commander into your hand from the command zone.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Llanowar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Sulfurous Springs deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}. Yavimaya Coast deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Battlefield Forge deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Shivan Reef deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Caves of Koilos deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{U/R}, {T}: Add {U}{U}, {U}{R}, or {R}{R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{W/B}, {T}: Add {W}{W}, {W}{B}, or {B}{B}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Add {R}. Put a stash counter on Glittering Stockpile.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Glittering Stockpile: Add X mana of any one color, where X is the number of stash counters on Glittering Stockpile.', '{T}: Add {R}.\\nAs Cursed Mirror enters the battlefield, you may have it become a copy of any creature on the battlefield until end of turn, except it has haste.', "{T}: Add {U}. When you spend this mana to cast an instant or sorcery spell with mana value 3 or less, you may exile that spell instead of putting it into its owner's graveyard as it resolves.\\n{3}{U}{U}, {T}: You may cast any number of spells from among cards exiled with Forger's Foundry without paying their mana costs. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{T}: Add {U}.\\n{2}{U}: Put an hour counter on Midnight Clock.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, put an hour counter on Midnight Clock.\\nWhen the twelfth hour counter is put on Midnight Clock, shuffle your hand and graveyard into your library, then draw seven cards. Exile Midnight Clock.', '{T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you created a token this turn.\\n{8}, {T}, Sacrifice Idol of Oblivion: Create a 10/10 colorless Eldrazi creature token.', '{T}: Draw two cards. Target opponent gains control of Humble Defector. Activate only during your turn.', '{T}: Mill two cards.\\n{2}, Exile Perpetual Timepiece: Shuffle any number of target cards from your graveyard into your library.']
flavor: ['"A little dirt doesn\'t indicate quality with goods or with people."', '"A little dirt doesn\'t indicate quality—with goods or with people."', '"Ah, another future archmage for my collection."', '"All matter, animate or not, rots when exposed to time. We merely speed up the process."\\n—Ezoc, Golgari rot farmer', '"Always bring a little extra thunder."', '"Arise, great one, and cleanse the world of our enemies!"', '"As Terisiare\'s mines ran dry, scrap metal became increasingly plentiful."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"Careful now. Don\'t want to get the seeds stuck to your feelers like last time."', '"Do not linger in such places, child. There the gwyllions dance. If they find you, you will join in their revels for eternity."\\n—Talara, elvish safewright', '"Either I know just the spell I need, or I\'m about to."', '"Every choice alters the path of fate."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Every seed holds strength and teaches patience."', '"Everyone\'s gotta die somehow. I\'ll be damned if I meet my end cowering in some cellar."', '"Everything serves a purpose. Even you."\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"Fire! Fire! Fire! What joy! What fire! Burn it all!"', '"For centuries my creation kept this world in balance. Now only her shadow remains."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"Get out of my way."', '"He may be a little green, but trust me, he\'s far from spineless."\\n—Yuma, proud protector', '"His tenement is filled with the most vile, disgusting vermin. It\'s infested with rats, too."\\n—Branko One-Ear', '"History remembers the conquerors, not the bones they stand on."\\n—Gonti', '"I adore your outfit. It\'s so . . . rustic."', '"I am not at liberty to reveal my sources, but I can assure you, the price on your head is high."', '"I bring a dawn that no night can follow."', '"I don\'t know what that is or who it belongs to, but it\'s shiny and I want it."', '"I gazed once into that light. Now it burns in my mind, forever denying me rest."\\n—Riku of Two Reflections', '"It reflects the purity of Mirrodin-that-was."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"It was a strange morning. When we awoke, we found our trees transformed. We didn\'t know whether to water them or polish them."\\n—Pulan, Bant orchardist', '"It\'s both an ingress-denial mechanism and an attractive hallway light!"\\n—Daxiver, Izzet electromancer', '"New growth applies a healing poultice to wounds long scabbed over."', '"Now *that\'s* how you strike gold!"\\n—Jolene, plundering pugilist', '"Now that\'s how you strike gold!"\\n—Jolene, plundering pugilist', '"Of course it works. What does it find? That\'s a surprise for a lucky buyer like yourself."\\n—Honest Rutstein', '"On vile wings and bloody wind, the swarm will rise."\\n—Skyclave inscription', '"Only the weak imprison themselves behind walls. We live free under the wind, and our freedom makes us strong."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"Sometimes the hardest choice is between two wonders."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"Survival rule 782: There are *always* more scute bugs."\\n—Zurdi, goblin shortcutter', '"That\'s a pretty ring! Trade you my knife for it."', '"The Great River will not be tamed."', '"The cost of your opposition will be extracted from your wits."\\n—Nekusar, the Mindrazer', '"The curse is broken."', '"The devils use fire. Why shouldn\'t we?"', '"The land grows only where the kami will it."\\n—Dosan the Falling Leaf', '"The seas are vast, but the skies are even more so. Why be content with one kingdom when I can rule them both?"', '"The specimen seems to be broken."', '"The sylex blast marked not only the end of the war, but the end of Dominaria as most knew it."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"The war polluted the land, turning what had once been fruitful fields into fetid morasses of mud and rusted corpses."\\n—*The Antiquities War*', '"The wilds are unpredictable. Rivers change course, trees shuffle and bend, rocks split and scurry. But mark my words, traveler—the main thing that\'ll change out there is *you*."\\n—Sturwynn, Boundary Lands ranger', '"There is great wisdom in rushing headlong into combat . . . if you\'re prepared."\\n—Kenjek, captain of the Thousand Swords', '"This must be the lost city of Zantafar, where my people lived before becoming nomads. Think of the history we\'ll learn here!"\\n—Quintorius, Lorehold mage-student', '"This world was once so much more than the confines of Naktamun."', '"To fill your mind with knowledge, we must start by emptying it."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Unimaginable riches? I assure you, I have a *vivid* imagination."', '"We give the audience what they want."\\n—Juri, proprietor of the Juri Revue', '"We have inherited the mysteries of the Thran, but few of the answers."\\n—Jhoira', '"We sail. We plunder. Then we dance."', '"Well, there\'s a good day\'s work ruined."\\n—Erin Nath, Omenport gravedigger', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"What say you, my most trusted advisors? . . . Advisors?"\\n—Edra, merfolk sovereign', '"What sort of life is that, huddling in the familiar and safe? No thanks. Put me right in the center of the action."', '"When all you have is a hammer, everything looks like a nail. I merely propose expanding our toolbox."', '"When gods become apathetic, the people will worship anyone who answers their pleas."\\n—Kiora', '"Who will miss you, drywalker? A wife? A child? Perhaps they will blame the sea for your fate, and teach future generations to stay far away from it."', '"You burn. I\'ll pillage."', '"You were once Mardu, so your body and will are strong. Now we must train your mind."\\n—Houn, Jeskai elder', '"Your own frailty is your undoing. I am merely the one to expose it."', '"Zendikar\'s wounds can be healed."', 'A blazing sun that never sets.', 'A captured elemental makes for a potent, albeit unstable, power source.', 'A mercurial face sows distrust. Distrust reaps a lonely life.', 'A smoldering storm of chilling fire.', 'Above the cries, a phrase rang out: "You will all be saved."', 'After lightning struck the cliffs, the ore became iron, the iron became steel, and the steel became greaves. The lightning never left.', "After seeing what the varmint was doing with her pocket watch, Elsa wasn't sure she even wanted it back.", 'After years of silence, the caves once again echo with the grisly sounds of Phyrexians preparing for war.', "All the money in the world won't buy back a pulse.", "An explorer's reward is a view of tomorrow's possibilities.", 'Anarchy comes in many forms: social, individual, Gruul . . .', 'Another imminent battle subsided in busy snuffling and carefree rooting.', "As magnigoth trees expanded across the sea into Almaaz and New Argive, it became clear Yavimaya's borders were never confined by its coastline.", "As the Eldrazi spread, no secret that could give Zendikar's defenders an advantage was considered too dangerous to seek.", 'As their roots soaked in a weak tea of bogwater and decay, the trees absorbed the essence of death into their living tissue.', 'At full moon, the river seeps over its banks and crawls through the woods like a blanket of serpents.', 'Automated systems at the Tolarian Academy sort new acquisitions for optimal use, determining which should be studied, eaten, or sold.', 'Beauty is in the eye of the exploder.', 'Better potent than predictable.', 'Blood magic is more artery than science.', "Captain Angrath cares less about treasure than mayhem. If he can't leave Ixalan, he'll burn the plane down.", 'Centuries of scouring sands have carved and polished the rocky terrain of the Shefet.', 'Chief among the tenets of Purphoros is that one must destroy in order to create.', 'Countless delights drift on the surface while dark schemes run below.', "Daniel's mistake wasn't just coming alone. It was believing his rival had done the same.", 'Dimir mages put the lanterns to good use, creating shapeshifters and sleeper agents from mana foreign to them.', 'Do not be so caught up in keeping track of time that you forget to make use of it.', 'Doyo suspected the boggarts of brewing a plot against his crop, so he scythed away his grain to clear the sightlines.', 'Every path leads to discovery.', 'Everything is flammable in the Burning Isles, even the mana itself.', 'Farmers cut the trees and buried their dead. The dead rose up and killed the farmers. The trees grew back and strangled the dead.', 'Fields of battle turn to fields of grain.', "Genius is finding the edge of what's possible, then jumping over it.", 'Get carried away.', 'Gnolls make offerings to sinister forces in the shadow-drenched chasms.', 'Gold buys death. Death earns gold.', 'Held aloft by metabolized magic, trygons are ravenous for sources of mystic fuel.', 'His fists fume with the decay of death, each strike a plague on the hearts of his enemies.', 'Hobs bury their kin far from home. They believe the dry, open ground keeps hags from stealing the bones and gwyllions from stealing the spirits.', 'Immolation is the sincerest form of flattery.', "In places where the sea meets the trees, it's easy to forget the darkness that rules most of Innistrad.", 'Infinite wisdom cannot be contained within a single mind.', "It bends not light but mana, aligning its chaotic currents into the sharp angles necessary for the mystic's purposes.", 'It started as a mere drop of water. The Magic Mirror crystallized it into much more.', "It's a one-ecosystem army.", "It's much easier to list the places they *haven't* been.", 'Its beak rends flesh and bone, exposing the tender marrow of dream.', 'Life and death mixing together, both ends of the same cycle giving rise to something else.', 'Made of bone and boiled in blood, a Rakdos signet is not considered finished until it has been used as a murder weapon.', 'Majesty rising above the arid sweep of land, a bulwark horizon against the mundane, a divide cleaving inspiration from stagnation.', 'Many hands for many evils.', 'Multiple pseudopods and no vital organs make dueling a whole lot easier.', 'Murky Otarian tides hide the forgotten treacheries of the Phyrexian war.', 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', 'No thought is as succulent as a secret.', 'None can tell how many vessels are tangled up on the sea floor—or how much treasure remains unclaimed.', 'Not every church is a place of faith.', "On Innistrad, one person's windfall usually starts with another person lying face down in the mud.", 'On Naya, ambition and treachery are scarce, hunted nearly to extinction by the awe owed to terrestrial gods.', 'On the continent of Tazeem, rushing waters plunge through narrow canyons into mist-cloaked lakes.', 'Once guarded by the Knights of the Reliquary, the tower stands now protected only by its own remoteness, its dusty treasures open to plunder by anyone.', 'Oriq agents stick to the dark corners of Arcavios, unseen yet ever-present.', 'Prismari students dance in the tension between passion and perfection.', 'Rumors float through the city like crows, alighting on citizens seemingly at random.', 'Rumors quickly spread among thieves about a labyrinth without walls and a prize beyond all measures of worth.', 'She follows the old tributaries built when merrows still shaped the tides.', 'Silence, the poetry of a whispering wind, the centurial fall of tar on pale sand.', 'Silent as a snowdrift. Inexorable as an avalanche.', 'Some Strixhaven study groups are more welcoming than others.', 'Some emeritus professors return from their wanderings periodically to share tales of the mystical wonders of Arcavios.', "Some naga initiates move as silently as the suns' reflections on the water.", 'Some spellcrafting mistakes go on to become spells of their own.', 'Stability and volatility churn together, creating beauty and danger both.', 'Still to the ignorant eye, yet bursting with life. A million actions and reactions, unstoppable as the dawn.', 'Street folk call them "spire mice," but behind the mockery is an unspoken envy of the ledgewalkers\' skill at avoiding harm.', 'Sunhome—the stalwart shield, the towering sentinel, the seat of justice.', 'Take two steps north into the unsettled future, south into the unquiet past, east into the present day, or west into the great unknown.', 'The Curse of Wandering permeated Amonkhet long before Nicol Bolas. He simply harnessed it.', "The Eldrazi don't merely extinguish life—they supplant it.", 'The Eldrazi hunger without limit and consume without pause.', 'The Izzet signet is redesigned often, each time becoming closer to a vanity portrait of Niv-Mizzet.', 'The Roil redraws the world as it passes, leaving only the hedrons unchanged.', 'The boiling seas around Shiv provided a welcome layer of protection for the reclaimed Mana Rig.', 'The continent of Guul Draz is a geothermal swampland reeking of heat and decay.', 'The crater screamed into the wind, and the wind carried its blazing voice across the sky.', 'The dense jungle surrenders to a lush and lavish expanse. At its center uncoil the spires of Qarsi Palace.', 'The first satyr to wake after a revel must search for the site of the next one.', "The guards kindled the hearth and locked the door to Ellwen's chamber. By morning, the fire was out and Ellwen was gone.", 'The new model has improved aerodynamics but introduced a few glitches in the targeting system.', 'The only thing Ziatora desires is "more."', 'The peace summit proved the grudge between Urza and Mishra could end only in blood.', 'The sigil holds different meanings depending on its form and presentation. While some wear it as a sign of status, others wear it as a sign of debt.', "The sunlight falls pristine on the temple at Epityr, softened by the remembered shadows of angelic saviors' wings.", 'The tower guards eventually gave up, figuring it was better at the job anyway.', 'There is a sanctuary that reveals itself only to those graced by the *eludha*—the mystical connection between bonder and monster.', 'Those who love the woods only wish to spread its majesty.', 'Tomorrow belongs to those who prepare for it today.', 'Travelers bathe in the falls to wash away curses from the pucas who lurk nearby.', "Ugin saw the gem that connected Bolas to his Meditation Realm as the key to his brother's downfall.", "Unaware of Lorwyn's diversity, it sees only itself, reflected a thousand times over.", "Under Drana's leadership, vampires are finding new strength in unity.", 'When asked how much power is required, Izzet mages always answer "more."', 'When defeat is near and guidance is scarce, all eyes look in one direction.', 'When its power is threatened, the council speaks with a unified voice.', "When killing five just isn't enough.", 'When the great vault fell, it scattered its wonders across Thunder Junction.', 'When the last scrap of flesh is scoured away, the Curse of Wandering ends. Then the dead may sleep.', 'When the ruins awakened, so did their defenses.', 'Where ambition meets industry, passion is poisoned by greed.', 'Where curiosity meets cruelty, hideous innovations arise.', 'With the Hekma breached and its protection removed, the deserts swept in.']
artist: ['A. M. Sartor', 'Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alayna Danner', 'Alex Konstad', 'Alexander Forssberg', 'Alix Branwyn', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Andrea Piparo', 'Andrew Mar', 'Andrey Kuzinskiy', 'Anna Pavleeva', 'Anna Podedworna', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Aurore Folny', 'Ben Hill', 'Ben Thompson', 'Ben Wootten', 'Billy Christian', 'Borja Pindado', 'Brad Rigney', 'Bram Sels', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Brian Valeza', 'Brock Grossman', 'Bruce Brenneise', 'Bryan Sola', 'Caio Monteiro', 'Campbell White', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Cold', 'Chris Ostrowski', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Christine Choi', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cristi Balanescu', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Danny Schwartz', 'Daren Bader', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Gaillet', 'Denman Rooke', 'Diana Cearley', 'Dmitry Burmak', 'Donato Giancola', 'E. M. Gist', 'Ekaterina Burmak', 'Eli Minaya', 'Erica Yang', 'Ernanda Souza', 'Evyn Fong', 'Fajareka Setiawan', 'Filip Burburan', 'Florian de Gesincourt', 'Fred Fields', 'Gaboleps', 'Grady Frederick', 'Greg Staples', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Heather Hudson', 'Heonhwa Choe', 'Howard Lyon', 'Iain McCaig', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Irina Nordsol', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jake Murray', 'Jakub Kasper', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'James Wong', 'James Zapata', 'Jason Felix', 'Jehan Choo', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jodie Muir', 'Johan Grenier', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'Jon Foster', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Joshua Raphael', 'Julian Kok Joon Wen', 'Jung Park', 'Kaitlyn McCulley', 'Kamila Szutenberg', 'Kari Christensen', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kekai Kotaki', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Kim Sokol', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Liiga Smilshkalne', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Livia Prima', 'Lorenzo Mastroianni', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Manuel Castañón', 'Mark Behm', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Winters', 'Marta Nael', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Ma